pagemap-diff

From: Victor Araújo <victor@victor-software-house.com>

Downstream-Reason: A diff snapshot without dirty tracking writes the pages the guest wrote, read from the host page tables, so boxes can restore without dirty logging and keep 2 MiB pages.
Upstream-Status: not-submitted
Drop-When: Upstream Firecracker takes a diff snapshot without dirty tracking from the page tables, and its jailer gives the jailed process its own /proc.
